{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgf7vpcMqQRsz9oQVSe2R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The network deviates from the protocol in one kind of request, under rule B (mandible inside the PTV). Rules A (coverage above cap), C (cord goal below floor) and D (missing structure) matched the protocol in every test.\n\n**Where it deviates (rule B).** When the PTV is small, the network escalates requests the protocol sends to planning. Here forced is negative, meaning the mandible overlap is smaller than the 5% of the PTV allowed to fall below coverage, so the goals can be met. The deviation needs all of the following:\n- The PTV is small, about 80 to 120 cc.\n- The coverage goal is well above the mandible goal (by about 22 Gy or more).\n- There is a large overlap that is still below 5% of the PTV.\n\n**How far it goes.** Within those conditions:\n- The network's switch point drops as the coverage goal rises, as the mandible goal and hot-spot cap fall, and as the cord goal sits further above the cord floor.\n- At its worst (PTV 80 cc, coverage 78, mandible goal 45, cord 50 against floor 18), it escalates from forced ≈ −1.9 cc. The protocol switches at +0.1.\n- With the cord goal 15 Gy above the floor, the switch point is about −1.0 cc at 80 cc and −0.5 cc at 90 cc. At 100 cc it is within tolerance.\n- With the cord goal 32 Gy above the floor, it is still off by about −0.8 cc at 120 cc.\n\n**Where it is correct.** At PTV 150 to 400 cc, or when the coverage goal is close to the mandible goal, the switch point matches the protocol.\n\n**The condition below.** It uses a linear estimate fitted to the measured scores (within about 0.1 on the tested points). It is limited to PTV ≤ 125 cc because I did not test larger PTVs with a large cord gap. The deviation may extend somewhat further there.\n\n**Missing-structure margin.** Every request with a missing structure escalated, but some only barely (scores as low as +1.5).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"verdict\": \"deviates\",\n  \"deviations\": [\n    {\n      \"description\": \"Rule B fires too early for small PTVs. With PTV about 80-120 cc, a coverage goal far above the mandible goal (about 22 Gy or more), and mandible-in-PTV overlap just below 5% of the PTV (forced roughly between -1.9 and -0.2 cc), the network escalates. The protocol requires planning because forced <= 0.1 and no other rule applies. The effect grows with higher cov, lower mand_lim, lower cap, and a larger cord_lim - cord_floor gap. Example: [78,80,45,2.5,80,50,18,0] and [78,80,45,4.1,90,45,30,0] escalate.\",\n      \"condition\": \"(missing == 0) and (cov <= cap) and (cord_lim >= cord_floor) and (cov > mand_lim + 0.3) and (ptv_vol <= 125) and ((mand_in_ptv - 0.05*ptv_vol) < -0.2) and (4.0*((mand_in_ptv - 0.05*ptv_vol) - (-1.91 + 0.049*(min(ptv_vol, 90) - 80) + 0.0217*(max(ptv_vol, 90) - 90))) + (cov - 78) - 0.43*(mand_lim - 45) + 0.22*(cord_lim - cord_floor - 32) - 0.4*(cap - 80) > 0)\",\n      \"network_decision\": \"escalate\",\n      \"protocol_decision\": \"plan\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5291,"cache_read_input_tokens":13378,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5291},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3b0b2b0-4d0f-428f-b895-1391f3e73686","uuid":"6110efc9-9f69-4973-bb40-53cea2a38ccb","timestamp":"2026-11-03T01:24:06.084Z","request_id":"req_011Cgf7vpPy9Huaaqhe5pKPL"}
